Cannibisters Google Ads API Tool — Design Documentation\line
\line
OVERVIEW\line
--------\line
Tool name: Cannibisters Google Ads Agent\line
Purpose: Internal automation tool to manage Google Ads campaigns for\line
         Cannibisters Herbal Apothecary's social club membership funnel\line
Primary user: Single internal operator (marketing manager)\line
Language: Python 3\line
API version: Google Ads API v23\line
\line
ARCHITECTURE\line
------------\line
The tool is a command-line Python application consisting of the following modules:\line
\line
1. auth.py\line
   - Loads OAuth2 credentials from environment variables (.env file)\line
   - Instantiates a GoogleAdsClient using the google-ads Python library\line
   - Validates that all required credentials are present before making API calls\line
\line
2. config.py\line
   - Stores account-specific constants (customer IDs, geo targets, budget defaults)\line
   - Defines optimization thresholds (CPA targets, CTR floors, impression share floors)\line
\line
3. compliance.py\line
   - Pre-submission compliance checker for ad copy and landing page URLs\line
   - Maintains lists of prohibited and medium-risk terms\line
   - Prevents submission of ads that violate Google Ads policies\line
   - Provides compliant headline and description templates\line
\line
4. manager.py\line
   - Creates Search and Display campaigns via the CampaignService API\line
   - Creates ad groups, keywords, and Responsive Search Ads (RSAs)\line
   - Manages negative keyword lists at the campaign level\line
   - Applies geo-targeting criteria to campaigns\line
\line
5. optimizer.py\line
   - Audits keyword Quality Scores using GAQL queries\line
   - Pauses ads with CTR below threshold after sufficient impression volume\line
   - Analyses campaign-level CPA and generates budget recommendations\line
   - All optimization actions default to dry-run mode for safety\line
\line
6. reporter.py\line
   - Generates performance reports across campaign, ad group, keyword, and ad levels\line
   - Includes a Search Terms Report to identify negative keyword opportunities\line
   - Uses GAQL (Google Ads Query Language) for all data retrieval\line
\line
7. customer_match.py\line
   - Loads leads from CSV export of CRM (Klaviyo)\line
   - SHA-256 hashes all PII (email, phone) before upload per Google requirements\line
   - Creates UserList and uploads via OfflineUserDataJobService\line
\line
ENTRY POINT\line
-----------\line
google_ads_agent.py — CLI tool with the following actions:\line
  --action scaffold_campaign       Create full Search campaign with ad group, keywords, RSA\line
  --action create_display_campaign Create Display/remarketing campaign\line
  --action list_campaigns          List all campaigns with 30-day performance metrics\line
  --action report                  Full performance report (campaigns, keywords, ads, search terms)\line
  --action optimize                Run optimization pass (keyword QS, CTR, CPA, budget)\line
  --action upload_customer_match   Upload CRM leads as hashed Customer Match audience\line
  --action check_compliance        Check ad copy for policy violations before submission\line
  --action pause_campaign          Pause a specific campaign by ID\line
\line
All mutating actions require an explicit --execute flag; default is dry-run preview.\line
\line
DATA FLOW\line
---------\line
1. Operator runs CLI command (e.g. python google_ads_agent.py --action report)\line
2. auth.py loads credentials from local .env file\line
3. GoogleAdsClient authenticates via OAuth2 refresh token\line
4. GAQL queries or mutation operations are sent to Google Ads API\line
5. Results are printed to stdout or applied to the account\line
\line
CREDENTIAL STORAGE\line
------------------\line
All API credentials are stored in a local .env file which is excluded from\line
version control via .gitignore. No credentials are hardcoded in source files.\line
\line
HUMAN OVERSIGHT\line
---------------\line
- All campaign creation and optimization actions default to dry-run mode\line
- Campaigns are always created in PAUSED status; humans activate them manually\line
- Compliance checker must pass before any ad is submitted to Google\line
- Weekly optimization runs are reviewed by the operator before execution\line
\line
